            <ArticleTitle>The clinical significance of microvascular impairment in patients with pure uncomplicated diabetes mellitus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>123-4; author reply 128</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pure uncomplicated type 2 diabetes mellitus is 'coronary artery disease equivalent' in view of microvascular impairment in myocardium. We believe that the current study reemphasized clinical significance of coronary microvasculature assesment in patients with diabetes mellitus even though they had normal luminogram.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
